A||N||4||Ozzy||Drive axles...||||5||
Z||000000||Ozzy||05-06-2000||08:59 PM||||Recently I posted my problem on the '88 Coupe 5 speed with a whiring kinda noise. Evryone's first thought was wheel bearings. I have checked them for play and rough movement and they seem fine on both sides. The toe alignment seems ok. I have no reason to suspect anything changed on the alignment and the bushings and links seem tight and o.k. <P>If the above are fine, whats left? Do the drive axle CV joints make this constant type of noise when worn? The noise kicks in around 30mph and increases with vehicle speed. The noise appears to come from more on the drivers side although it's hard to tell for sure. I can move the drivers side axle in and out about a tad over 1/8".  <P>How would I tell if it is a tranny bearing? Also, one of the axle seals is leaking at the tranny. Can these be replaced with the tranny in the vehicle?          <P>TIA<P>Ozzy   ||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroGTGirl||05-07-2000||01:38 AM||||Ozzy~~<P>Same symptoms exactly on my Fiero couple months ago...<P>We had a mechanic look at it(a little too late) and he diagnosed that the hub assembly was bad and the leak was an inner seal leak that had been neglected.  Consequently, he drained the transaxle fluid and found to our delight  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> metal shavings in what fluid was left...<P>Hope you find your solution before it gets to that point because that is spendy and NO fun...<P>Good Luck<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ozzy||05-07-2000||02:10 AM||||Hmmmm...'GTgirl, that'd be a bummer on the GT for sure. The Getrag is not cheap to fix. Fortunately this is on my Coupe which has the Isuzu 5 spd. They are fairly easy to find and cheap. <P>The hub assy. thing is what I was already looking at, but I'll be damned if it acts like a bad bearing type problem. Usually you can feel a bad bearing but these feel fine. The replacement hub is around $80 from the Fiero store if memory serves me but I want to be sure what it is first...<P>Ozzy||||reg||9
Z||000003||Phaeton||05-07-2000||05:55 AM||||What kind of shape are those rubber flap dust controller thingies in? could part of one be blowing against the joint assembly only at speed?<P>Shiny spots anywhere?<P>Fiero bearings are sometimes sneaky little boogers and feel just fine right up to and past the end of their deceptive lives.<P>Then again, lots of lttle sliding rings in trannies to clink and whirr, perhaps harmlessly?||||reg||12
Z||000004||jfuredy||05-09-2000||02:16 PM||||I got a new hub assembly for my 88 from Autozone (or maybe Checker) for $40-50.  It was a Timken unit that worked fine.  My symptoms were exactly the same as yours: no noise at low speed, then increasingly annoying at higher speeds.<P>Good luck with it,<BR>Joe Furedy||||reg||1
